  "name": "IVX Holdings v1.10.20 (QA) — Live E2E audit fixes + persistent crash log",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": false,
  "body": "Live end-to-end audit run against **production**, not a code read. Findings and fixes below.\n\n## Live audit results\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Supabase auth health | **200 OK** |\n| Owner sign-in (`iperez4242@gmail.com`) | **200 OK** — access token issued, correct user id |\n| `profiles` query with owner token | **200 OK** — rows returned |\n| `notifications` query with owner token | **200 OK** — rows returned |\n| `IVX_OWNER_PASSWORD` stored in Render env | **400 Invalid login credentials** |\n\nBackend, auth, and data are healthy. The black screen is **not** a server, auth, or RLS failure — that entire class is now eliminated by execution rather than assumption.\n\n## Defect found and fixed: React hook called outside render\n\n`lib/ota-error-handler.ts` line 104 called:\n\n```ts\nconst currentUpdate = updates.useUpdates?.()?.currentlyRunning;\n```\n\n`useUpdates()` is a **React hook**. This function is `async` and runs from an effect continuation, so React's hook dispatcher is not installed — the call throws on **every single launch**.\n\nWorse: if the awaited `import('expo-updates')` resolves while React happens to be rendering, the hook registers into whatever component is mid-render and **permanently corrupts that component's hook order**. That produces \"Rendered more hooks than during the previous render\" — a non-deterministic crash that fires shortly after a screen paints, which matches the reported timing.\n\nFixed by reading the same values from plain module constants, plus an early return when updates are disabled (they are: `updates.enabled: false`), so no update code runs in production at all.\n\n## Persistent crash log — this ends the blind loop\n\nThe black screen destroyed its own evidence: JS teardown killed every in-memory log, which is why runtime logs have been empty this entire investigation.\n\nNew `lib/crash-log.ts` writes the fatal error to device storage the instant it happens. On the next launch the app shows a **Previous Crash Detected** screen with the message, stack trace, build stamp, and timestamp.\n\nEven if a future failure still manages to blank the screen, **relaunching the app now reports exactly what happened.** The failure can no longer erase its own evidence.\n\n## Verified in shipped assets/index.android.bundle\n\n| Marker | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Previous Crash Detected` | present |\n| `ivx_last_fatal_crash` | present |\n| `recordCrash` / `readLastCrash` | present |\n| `IVX Runtime Error` (fatal shield) | present |\n| `IVX Render Error` (render boundary) | present |\n| `1.10.20 (118)` build stamp | present |\n| `useUpdates?.()` hook bug | **REMOVED** |\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): 0 errors\n- Test suite: 1136 pass, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures\n- Gradle: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 1m 32s`\n\nversionName 1.10.20 / versionCode 118\nSHA256: `23f5a2e9bc091d31b2bdd5a54c0d88858240b430cf9431168f69eafca931a45f`"
}
